build: 2026-06-28 v10.76.44 (Own number pad — − / + bottom-left, same everywhere)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.43. Reworks number entry. The iOS number pad can't carry a sign
  key, and the old "± in the keyboard bar" was unintuitive for Transpose. So Echoel now has
  its OWN keypad (EchoelNumberPad) with a MINUS and a PLUS at the bottom-left, used by EVERY
  numeric field in the app (FX, synth, mix, bio, transpose, tempo…) — one consistent control
  ("alles angeglichen"). − makes the value negative, + makes it positive: for Transpose, type
  5 then tap − → −5. On fields that can't go below zero (Hz, BPM) the − key is simply greyed
  out. Drag-up/down on a value still adjusts it as before; tapping a value now opens this pad
  (tap is more reliable now — the old 1 pt drag threshold that sometimes swallowed taps was
  raised). VoiceOver unchanged. Reviewed for compile-safety AND SwiftUI state-flow (the many
  per-field sheets do NOT risk the launch crash — each lives on its own small view, not the
  root body): both GO.
  Test: 10.76.44 → Transpose: tap the value, type 5, tap − → shows −5, OK. Tap any Hz/BPM
  value → − is greyed (positive-only). Same pad layout everywhere. Still launches to Studio,
  dropdowns stay selectable.
